{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-115474",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Since $y$ varies inversely with $x,$ we use the equation\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{k}{x}.\n$$\n\nNext, we use the given data $y=9$ when $x=-4$ to find $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9 & =\\frac{k}{(-4)} \\\\ 9\\cdot (-4) & =k \\\\ -36 & =k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our inverse variation equation is\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{36}{x}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
